PixelPilot: Scalable Vision-Language-Action Models for End-to-End Autonomous Driving
nuScenes source release 0.2.0, prepared 2026-11-05.

This release is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Existing
copyright/license notices apply to their respective components and are retained.

The bundled LLaMAFactory source is the locally supplied
LLaMA-Factory-0.9.4 research snapshot. Its internal version is 0.9.4.dev0.
Copyright notices credit the LlamaFactory team, HuggingFace Inc. and other
original contributors where present. Its upstream Apache license is retained
both with the source and under licenses/.

The verl/ package and checkpoint merger come from the supplied Seg-Zero-main
snapshot, based on Seg-Zero, EasyR1 and veRL. Original Bytedance and other
contributor notices are preserved. The recovered nuScenes planning/map helper
files preserve NVIDIA and nuScenes-devkit copyright/license notices.
No exact upstream commit identifier was supplied for either research snapshot.
Original source SHA-256 values are recorded in docs/source_manifest.json.

Release adaptations include configurable local paths; deterministic multi-task
sampling; extracted projection helpers; SFT/GRPO data validation and registration;
a portable SFT configuration derived from a supplied two-epoch experiment;
explicit use of the bundled SFT framework; lazy/calibration-cached GRPO rewards;
a null validation-data field; empty-response handling; the training-step stop
boundary correction; local-only checkpoint merging; explicit inference image
pixel limits; resumable teacher candidate generation and new conditioning,
selection and SFT attachment glue; id-aligned metric wrappers with explicit
frames and denominators; source audit, tests, CI and reproducible exports.
The unused red-light helper requiring missing expand_lane code is omitted.
Modified upstream files carry modification notices. Original metric equations
and the historical GRPO reward formula are retained, with limitations documented.

This source license does not grant rights to separately obtained datasets,
teacher services or pretrained model weights. No dataset/weight/log artifacts
are included in the source export.
